<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Liberia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1851">1851</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Liberia College</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of Liberia, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a>, is the country's main public university. It was chartered in 1851 as Liberia College, opened in 1862, and became a university in 1951. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-wilmot-blyden">Edward Wilmot Blyden</a> taught there and served as its president, and many of Liberia's leaders studied there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-liberia.jpg" alt="University of Liberia" width="225" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: University of Liberia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UL_LOGO.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
